  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1407.05 Delivery",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1407.05 Delivery.\n\n(a) A used oil transporter shall deliver all used oil received to the following entities provided the entity has obtained an EPA identification number:\n\n(1) Another used oil transporter, subject to (b), below;\n\n(2) A used oil processor/re-refiner; or\n\n(3) A used oil burner.\n\n(b) For the purposes of (a)(1), above, if the transfer occurs within New Hampshire:\n\n(1) The used oil transporter receiving the used oil shall also possess a current and valid New Hampshire hazardous waste transporter registration; and\n\n(2) The transfer shall occur at either a used oil transfer facility or a permitted hazardous waste transfer facility.\n\n(c) If a shipment of used oil subject to regulation under this chapter is accompanied by a manifest, the NH01 hazardous waste number shall not be recorded on the manifest.\n\nSource. #14282, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html"
